   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "mean_variety_country = filtered_pumpkins.groupby(['country','variety'])['weight_in_kg'].mean()\n",
    "print(mean_variety_country) #Groups by country and calculates mean value and then prints"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "55a349ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Next to get the lowest mean weight variety we can do:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "c9a058e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The lowest mean weight was 'Early Giant' from Japan, weighing 69.8kg.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "lowest_mean_row = mean_variety_country.idxmin() #Gets lowest row (country, variety)\n",
    "lowest_mean_value = mean_variety_country.min() #Gets lowest mean weight value\n",
    "print(f\"The lowest mean weight was '{lowest_mean_row[1]}' from {lowest_mean_row[0]}, weighing {round(lowest_mean_value,2)}kg.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "03ec31fe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 8 - Weight Distribution Boxplot 📊\n",
    "\n",
    "### Creating a boxplot"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "fig-weight_boxplot",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 672x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
       "height": 439,
       "width": 618
      }
     },
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "#| label: fig-weight_boxplot\n",
    "#| fig-cap: A boxplot showing the distribution of pumpkin weight of three countries from the filtered pumpkin competitions dataset.\n",
    "figure_3 = plt.figure() #Creates a new figure\n",
    "plot_area_3 = figure_3.add_subplot() #Creates new plotting area in figure\n",
    "filtered_pumpkins.boxplot(column = 'weight_in_kg', by = 'country', ax = plot_area_3)\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"\") #Removes pandas title so I can add my own\n",
    "plot_area_3.set_title(\"Boxplot of Weight distribution by country\")\n",
    "plot_area_3.set_xlabel('Country')\n",
    "plot_area_3.set_ylabel('Pumpkin Weight (kg)');"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4e787fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Saving the boxplot\n",
    "This boxplot can now be saved by running:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "dcda3573",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: true\n",
    "figure_3.savefig(\"filtered_boxplot.png\", dpi = 300) #Saves the third figure (boxplot) to disk. Increased dpi to improve readability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "13aa12b1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### What does the boxplot show?\n",
    "In @fig-weight_boxplot the distribution of pumpkin weight in kg of the three countries (United Kingdom, Japan and Italy) can be seen. \n",
    "\n",
    "Looking at the three boxes, it is seen that Italy produced the heighest overall weighted pumpkins, as its median is higher than both Japan and the United Kingdom.\n",
    "Italy also has a large number of outliers\n",
    "\n",
    "Japan produces the lowest weighted pumpkins as its median is below both of the other countries. It also has the lowest interquartile range of the countries, showing\n",
    "low variability. Japan also has the least number of outliers.\n",
    "\n",
    "The United Kingdom produces pumpkins weighted in between the other countries based on its median value. It has a similar number of outliers to Italy but at lower weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Task 9 - Facet Plot 📉\n",
